ConcurrentStack<T> is a concurrent version of Stack<T> and implements
the IProducerConsumerCollection<T> interface. We can push or pop items from the
stack, which works in the Last In, First Out (LIFO) format. It doesn't involve kernel-level
locking, rather it relies on spinning and compare-and-swap operations to remove any
contention.
